.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt COOK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cook
.Nd rebuild the next and seen merge branches
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
rebuilds two merge branches in a
.Xr jj 1
repository, in the style of git.git's integration branches.
Topics flow from
.Sy seen
to
.Sy next
to trunk.
.Pp
The description of the
.Sy next
commit lists the topics of both branches, one per line, below a line
that reads
.Li [cook] .
Text above that line is free prose, such as a title and notes.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
next <ref>
seen <ref>
.Ed
.Pp
A
.Ar ref
is any revision that names a topic: a local bookmark, a remote
bookmark such as
.Li foo@origin ,
a commit id, or a change id.
It is resolved each time
.Nm
runs, so a topic named by a bookmark follows the bookmark as it moves,
and a topic named by a change id follows the change as it is
rewritten.
Name a topic by its commit id to keep merging exactly that commit.
Since a
.Ar ref
is a revset, it must resolve to exactly one commit.
.Pp
A
.Ql #
starts a comment, which runs to the end of the line.
A comment can label a topic named by an id, such as with the bookmark
it came from.
.Pp
.Nm
rebases
.Sy next
onto
.Li trunk()
and each
.Sy next
topic, in the order listed.
It then rebases
.Sy seen
onto
.Sy next
and each
.Sy seen
topic.
A branch with no topics sits on its base alone.
After each rebase,
.Nm
removes the branch's redundant parents.
A topic that has landed on trunk is dropped, and so is a base that a
topic already contains.
A topic listed under both
.Sy next
and
.Sy seen
is merged into
.Sy next
only.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n
Print the
.Xr jj 1
commands instead of running them.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
It fails, and changes nothing, if the description of
.Sy next
has no
.Li [cook]
line, or if a line below it, less any comment, is not blank and is not a
.Li next
or
.Li seen
line with exactly one
.Ar ref .
It also fails if a topic does not name exactly one commit.
If any rebase fails,
.Nm
restores the repository to the operation it started from, so that
.Sy next
and
.Sy seen
move together or not at all.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A description of
.Sy next
that merges one local topic, one remote topic, and one topic pinned to
a commit, and stages a fourth topic in
.Sy seen :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
next

[cook]
next fix-parser
next feature@origin
next 3f1c2a9e # other-feature@origin
seen experiment  # needs tests
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jj 1
